    "problem_statement": "# SVG string encoding issue with QR code generation\n\nI'm having an issue with the SVG fragment image generation in the qrcode library. When trying to compare the saved SVG content with the string representation, I'm getting unexpected behavior.\n\n## What I expected\n\nI expected that the content saved to a file-like object would be contained within the string representation returned by `to_string()`.\n\n## What happened instead\n\nThe comparison fails, suggesting that the encoding of the SVG content is different between the two methods.\n\nHere's a simple reproduction script:\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nimport io\nfrom qrcode.image.svg import SvgFragmentImage\n\n# Create a QR code with some Unicode text\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data(\"Hello, 世界!\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=SvgFragmentImage)\n\n# Save to a file-like object\nfile_like = io.BytesIO()\nimg.save(file_like)\nfile_like.seek(0)\nsaved_content = file_like.read()\n\n# Get string representation\nstring_content = img.to_string()\n\n# Check if saved content is in string representation\nprint(\"Saved content in string representation:\", saved_content in string_content)\nprint(\"Type of saved content:\", type(saved_content))\nprint(\"Type of string representation:\", type(string_content))\n```\n\nThe issue seems to be related to how the XML string is being encoded/decoded in the `to_string()` method. The saved content is bytes, but the string representation is being converted to a string with a specific encoding, causing the comparison to fail.\n\n## System Information\n\n```json\n{\n  \"qrcode\": {\n    \"version\": \"7.4.2\"\n  },\n  \"implementation\": {\n    \"name\": \"CPython\",\n    \"version\": \"3.10.15\"\n  },\n  \"platform\": {\n    \"system\": \"Linux\"\n  }\n}\n```"
  }
